                <pb facs="0656" n="584" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg584"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/173.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Sultan of Turkey to the President of the United
                        States.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-04-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I received with real pleasure the telegram of congratulation which Your
                    Excellency was pleased to send me on the occasion of my accession to the throne.
                    I thank you cordially for the sentiments contained therein, as well as for the
                    assurances of friendship which you give me in the name of the Government and the
                    great Nation of the United States, and to which I attach the highest value. I
                    beg of Your Excellency to believe in the cordial wishes which I cherish both for
                    your happiness and prosperity and for those of the great, noble American
                    people.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mohammed V.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
